# Two reactant patterns that match one complex, with the molecularity checks off.
#
# Bind joins the r site of one A to the l site of another, and Unbind breaks
# such a bond again. With -no-bscb, Bind may join two A that are already in
# one chain, closing it into a ring. When a firing changes molecules, NFsim
# lists them, and the molecules near them, to take them out of the
# observables and put them back. The list is built by walking out from each
# reactant to a limit. Two A in one chain can lie beyond each other's limit
# with the stretch between them inside both, and NFsim listed that stretch
# twice and put it back into the Molecules observables twice.
#
# Nothing makes or removes an A, so Atot is 30 at every sample, with or
# without -no-bscb. With -no-bscb NFsim ended between 66 and 111 at 40 seeds.

begin model
begin parameters
  kf  1.0
  kb  1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(l,r)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(l,r)   30
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Atot  A()
end observables
begin reaction rules
  Bind:   A(r) + A(l) -> A(r!1).A(l!1)   kf
  Unbind: A(r!1).A(l!1) -> A(r) + A(l)   kb
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
